# P3-1 Task 6 fixture (-hide, design doc §1a/§1b, ruling R1).
#
# Declares module `hide_owner` and hides the atom `hide_secret`.  Companion
# fixtures: `hide_other.clausal` (a DIFFERENT module declaring the SAME
# bare spelling globally, NOT hidden -- cross-module isolation) and
# `hide_importer.clausal` (imports `holds/1` FROM this module but still
# cannot spell `hide_secret` itself -- see tests/test_hide_directive.py).
#
# `-strict_atoms` exercises the "strictness interplay" build requirement:
# `-hide` entries count as DECLARED for strictness purposes even though
# every reference here compiles to the mangled spelling, not the bare one
# -- every bare `hide_secret` reference below must compile clean under
# strict mode with no separate `-module`/`-private` listing of the name.

-strict_atoms
-module(hide_owner, [holds/1, label/1, same/2])
-hide([hide_secret])

holds(hide_secret),
label(hide_secret),

same(X, Y) <- (holds(X), label(Y)),
